WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.880
They met in the dissection hall at Prague and recognized each other at once as the

2
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.940
same kind of person.

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.940
They married, came to the United States in 1922, and ran into the rules of the era

4
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.860
head on. a Buffalo institute director ordered Gerty to stop publishing with her

5
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.820
husband, and she refused; at Washington University she was hired at a tenth of

6
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.300
Carl's salary for 16 years under nepotism rules.

7
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.090
The Cori cycle came out of work they did on the side of the tumor metabolism they

8
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.330
were paid to study: muscle breaks glucose to lactate, the blood carries the lactate

9
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.770
to the liver, and the liver spends energy to rebuild glucose.

10
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.150
Chasing a fraction everyone else discarded, they found the glycogen debranching

11
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:52.270
enzyme, and Gerty read its chromatography spot instantly and ran down the hall

12
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.170
shouting, "It's free glucose, it's free glucose!"

13
00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:00.850
the same free glucose that this chapter's last enzyme, glucose-6 -phosphatase,

14
00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:01.970
releases to the blood.

15
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:07.373
She went further, matching the wrong-shaped glycogen in sick children to specific

16
00:01:07.373 --> 00:01:12.073
missing enzymes: the first proof that one broken enzyme can cause an inherited

17
00:01:12.073 --> 00:01:13.073
disease.

18
00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:18.367
When the Nobel came in 1947, Carl used the banquet to center Gerty.

19
00:01:18.847 --> 00:01:23.347
The same year, dying of the myelofibrosis she had worked through for a decade, she

20
00:01:23.347 --> 00:01:25.067
was finally made a full professor.
